The TRC's report contained recommendations for the Province and the Federal Government, including calls to action aimed at addressing the legacy of the schools. These include:
Improving Indigenous child and family services and increasing Indigenous adoption placements in Ontario;
Increasing the number of Indigenous youth and senior adults receiving First Nation and Inuit social services to meet the specific needs of these populations;
Improving First Nation and Inuit health and social services to improve the health and well-being of First Nations and Inuit communities;
Improving First Nation and Inuit education to improve the educational outcomes of First Nation and Inuit children.
The Province of Ontario is committed to implementing all of the recommendations. We are working with Indigenous partners in Ontario to address many of the TRC's calls to action. The Government of Canada has committed to implementing all of the TRC's calls to action
